    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Each player is dealt 5 cards face-down and keeps them hidden. Play proceeds clockwise. On your turn you either make a bid or call Dudo. A bid states a quantity and a rank (e.g. Five Kings), meaning you believe that many cards of that rank (Aces often count as wild) exist across all players' hands. Each new bid must be higher: either a greater quantity or the same quantity of a higher rank. If you call Dudo you challenge the last bid; everyone reveals their hands. If the bid is correct the bidder wins the round and the challenger loses one card; if wrong the challenger wins and the bidder loses one card. The last player left with at least one card wins.",
    Player: "Each player is dealt 5 cards face-down and keeps them hidden. Play proceeds clockwise. On your turn you either make a bid or call Dudo. A bid states a quantity and a rank (e.g. Five Kings), meaning you believe that many cards of that rank (Aces often count as wild) exist across all players' hands. Each new bid must be higher: either a greater quantity or the same quantity of a higher rank. If you call Dudo you challenge the last bid; everyone reveals their hands. If the bid is correct the bidder wins the round and the challenger loses one card; if wrong the challenger wins and the bidder loses one card. The last player left with at least one card wins.",
    objective: 'Be the last player remaining with cards in your hand.',
    gameplay: "Each player is dealt 5 cards face-down and keeps them hidden. Play proceeds clockwise. On your turn you either make a bid or call Dudo. A bid states a quantity and a rank (e.g. Five Kings), meaning you believe that many cards of that rank (Aces often count as wild) exist across all players' hands. Each new bid must be higher: either a greater quantity or the same quantity of a higher rank. If you call Dudo you challenge the last bid; everyone reveals their hands. If the bid is correct the bidder wins the round and the challenger loses one card; if wrong the challenger wins and the bidder loses one card. The last player left with at least one card wins.",
    keyRules: [
      'Deal 5 cards each, all face-down and hidden.',
      'Bid a quantity and rank (e.g. Three 7s); each bid must be higher quantity or same quantity higher rank.',
      'Aces are usually wild and count as the bid rank.',
      'Call Dudo to challenge; all reveal; loser of the challenge discards one card.',
      'Last player with cards wins.',
